Estimate the area under $y=x^2+3$ from $x=0$ to $x=2$ using four midpoint rectangles. The dots mark where each height is read.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=2cm,y=0.65cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black] (0,0) rectangle (0.5,3.0625);
\draw[black] (0.5,0) rectangle (1,3.5625);
\draw[black] (1,0) rectangle (1.5,4.5625);
\draw[black] (1.5,0) rectangle (2,6.0625);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(2.3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,8) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,thick,domain=0:2,samples=50] plot (\x,{\x*\x+3});
\foreach \x/\y in {0.25/3.0625,0.75/3.5625,1.25/4.5625,1.75/6.0625} {\fill[black] (\x,\y) circle (1.5pt);}
\foreach \x in {0.5,1,1.5,2} {\draw[black] (\x,0.1)--(\x,-0.1);\path (\x,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\x$};}
\path (0,0) node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$0$};
\path (1,7.5) node {$y=x^2+3$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A car has velocity $v(t)=10+t^2$ metres per second for $0\leq t\leq3$ seconds. Use three left-endpoint rectangles to estimate how far it travels.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1.4cm,y=0.22cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black] (0,0) rectangle (1,10);
\draw[black] (1,0) rectangle (2,11);
\draw[black] (2,0) rectangle (3,14);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(3.5,0) node[right] {$t$ (s)};
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,22) node[above] {$v$ (m/s)};
\draw[black,thick,domain=0:3,samples=50] plot (\x,{10+\x*\x});
\foreach \x in {1,2,3} {\draw[black] (\x,0.4)--(\x,-0.4);\path (\x,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\x$};}
\path (0,0) node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$0$};
\path (1.5,21) node {$v=10+t^2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
